{title: Nothing but the Blood}
{artist: Robert Lowry}
{key: G}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune PLAINFIELD - Robert Lowry (1876)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1876, tune 1876: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
What can [G]wash away my sin? Nothing but the blood of [D]Jesus;
What can [G]make me whole again? [C]Nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
O! [C]precious is the [G]flow that makes me white as [D]snow;
No [G]other fount I know, [C]nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For my [G]pardon this I see, nothing but the blood of [D]Jesus;
For my [G]cleansing this my plea, [C]nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
This is [G]all my hope and peace, nothing but the blood of [D]Jesus;
This is [G]all my righteousness, [C]nothing but the [D]blood of [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
